# .chezmoiignore - files/dirs chezmoi should not manage.
#
# ~/.ssh is a one-time setup on this laptop (hostname "aditya"): the private
# key is templated from Bitwarden (private_dot_ssh/private_id_ed25519.tmpl
# calls the `bitwarden` template function), which forces a vault unlock on
# every `chezmoi diff`/`status`/`apply` even though the key never changes.
# Ignoring it here stops that - but only on this host, so a fresh machine
# bootstrapped from this same repo still gets the key populated once.
{{- if eq .chezmoi.hostname "aditya" }}
.ssh
.config/mise/config.toml
.config/foot/foot.ini
{{- end }}

# ~/.config/bws/access-token holds the live bws (Bitwarden Secrets Manager)
# machine-account token - see CHEZMOI-GUIDE.md's Bitwarden section. It's
# never supposed to be chezmoi-managed on any host (unlike the entries
# above, this applies everywhere, not just "aditya"). Verified with a real
# `chezmoi add` (v2.72.0, incl. `-r` on the whole ~/.config/bws dir and
# with `--force`): a path matched here is actually skipped, not just
# warned about - "chezmoi: warning: ignoring ..." and no file is written
# to the source state. So this line is real protection on its own, even
# before the root .gitignore's backstop below kicks in.
.config/bws/access-token

# ~/.claude (Claude Code's own global config dir) is a default-DENY
# allowlist, not a named block-list, because it holds a live OAuth
# credential (.credentials.json) alongside genuinely portable config
# (settings.json, custom themes). Added 2026-09-06 after actually copying
# the real ~/.claude tree into a connected folder and inspecting it file
# by file - this is what was actually found there, not assumed from docs:
#   - .credentials.json           - live OAuth token, never chezmoi-managed
#   - history.jsonl, .last-cleanup, backups/, cache/, projects/,
#     session-env/, sessions/, shell-snapshots/                - session/
#     app state Claude Code manages itself (transcripts under projects/
#     are plaintext and can contain secrets a tool read mid-session -
#     see CHEZMOI-GUIDE.md's ~/.claude section)
#   - plugins/                    - installed-plugin cache, managed by
#     `claude plugin` commands, not hand-edited
#   - chrome/chrome-native-host   - auto-generated by Claude Code itself
#     ("do not edit manually"), hardcodes this machine's exact mise-
#     installed binary path and version
#   - hooks/herdr-agent-state.sh  - installed and overwritten by herdr's
#     own integration ("managed by herdr" per its own header comment) -
#     managing it here would fight herdr's next reinstall/update
#   - skills/diagnose-crash, skills/omarchy - symlinks into
#     /usr/share/omarchy/default/agents/skills/ - Omarchy's own package
#     content, already present on any Omarchy install, nothing to sync
# Only settings.json and themes/ are chezmoi-managed (as
# home/dot_claude/settings.json.tmpl and home/dot_claude/themes/). The
# allowlist shape (ignore everything, then explicitly un-ignore the two
# safe paths) means a future Claude Code version adding some new file
# under ~/.claude is excluded by default too, not silently swept in by an
# accidental `chezmoi add -r ~/.claude`. Verified with the real chezmoi
# v2.72.0 binary against a scratch $HOME reproducing this exact directory
# structure: `chezmoi add -r ~/.claude`, including with `--force` and
# direct (non -r) adds targeting .credentials.json and the herdr hook
# script individually, all correctly skip everything except the two
# allowlisted paths - confirmed nothing else lands in source state.
.claude/**
!.claude
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/themes
!.claude/themes/**
# skills/ is NOT a `.claude/skills/**` wildcard allow, on purpose -
# skills/diagnose-crash and skills/omarchy above are Omarchy's own
# symlinked package content, and anything else Claude Code itself drops
# in this directory later should stay ignored by default too. Only
# specific, named personal skills (chezmoi-managed as
# home/dot_claude/skills/symlink_<name>, materializing the real content
# from home/dot_agents/skills/<name>/ - see CHEZMOI-GUIDE.md's
# "agent-agnostic skills" section) get un-ignored, one line per skill.
!.claude/skills
!.claude/skills/clojure-style
